<title>ITALY: Ciampi wants lira in ERM above 1,000/mark - papers.</title>
<headline>Ciampi wants lira in ERM above 1,000/mark - papers.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi was quoted as saying the government wanted to apply later this month to put the lira back into Europe's exchange rate mechanism at &quot;slightly above 1,000 per mark.&quot;</p>
<p>Ciampi, quoted by Italian newspapers citing an interview with Germany's Welt am Sonntag, said: &quot;We want to take the lira back into the ERM at an exchange rate slightly above 1,000 per mark.&quot;  </p>
<p>Ciampi, quoted in La Repubblica and La Stampa newspapers, told Welt am Sonntag: &quot;We will ask for re-entry for the lira in the (ERM) as soon as the budget debate in parliament is concluded, so in mid-November.&quot;</p>
<p>The lira left the ERM in a currency crisis in September 1992 and has floated freely ever since.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
